1. What you may do without asking

   a. Download the mod from this repository's Releases page, or from another
      place the author has published it, and install and play it for your
      own personal, non-commercial use.
   b. Read the source code on GitHub and learn from it.
   c. Make and share videos, streams, screenshots and reviews of you playing
      the mod.
   d. Share links to this repository or its Releases page.

   GitHub's Terms of Service also let GitHub users view this repository and
   fork it on GitHub. A fork on GitHub may be used only for that purpose and
   for offering changes back to this repository through pull requests. It
   does not give any of the rights listed in section 2.

2. What needs the author's written permission first

   Unless the author has given you permission in writing, you may not:

   a. copy all or part of the code, assets or text into another project,
      mod or game, whether or not it is for BeamNG.drive;
   b. modify the mod and share, publish or upload the modified version;
   c. re-upload, mirror, bundle or redistribute the mod, in original or
      modified form, including in modpacks;
   d. sell the mod, or use it in anything sold or paid for; or
   e. sublicense any part of it.

3. How to ask

   Open an issue on this repository
   (https://github.com/MadMerick01/beamng-worldwide-trucking-career-dangerous-contracts/issues)
   or contact MadMerick01 through GitHub. Say what you want to use and how.
   Permission counts only if the author gives it in writing, and it covers
   only what the author agreed to.

4. Contributions

   If you send a pull request or other contribution, you agree that the
   author may use, change and publish it as part of this project under this
